{"id":"colombia-andes-moto","title":"Colombia: coffee country to the Trampolín de la Muerte","who":"Classic route · the Colombian Andes by motorcycle","when":"December–March and June–August (drier)","vehicle":"Motorcycle, 10–14 days","kind":"moto","color":"#d97706","summary":"From Medellín south through colonial villages and the green hills of the coffee region, past Salento and the giant wax palms of the Cocora valley, down the Cauca valley to San Agustín's stone statues, and the famous dirt road of the Trampolín de la Muerte to Mocoa at the edge of the Amazon.","sources":[{"label":"Upshift: the Colombia experience, part 2","url":"https://upshiftonline.com/blogs/content/the-colombia-experience-part-2"},{"label":"JB's Trails: riding Colombian jungle roads","url":"https://jbstrails.com/?p=9121"}],"approximate":"A common route; the roads are the router's choice.","km":1065,"bbox":[-76.648,1.1465,-75.5067,6.2697],"stops":[{"name":"Medellín","place":"Medellín, Colombia","at":[6.2697,-75.6026],"text":"The city of eternal spring.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Centro_de_Medell%C3%ADn_en_dron_04.jpg/500px-Centro_de_Medell%C3%ADn_en_dron_04.jpg","page":"Medellín","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Centro_de_Medell%C3%ADn_en_dron_04.jpg","credit":"Juan Gómez","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Jardín","place":"Jardín, Antioquia","at":[5.5991,-75.8192],"text":"A colourful coffee village with a big church on the square."},{"name":"Manizales","place":"Manizales, Colombia","at":[5.0669,-75.5067],"text":"A ridge-top city under the Nevado del Ruiz volcano.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Manizales_Montage_L.jpg/500px-Manizales_Montage_L.jpg","page":"Manizales","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manizales_Montage_L.jpg","credit":"JSJS07 (compilation, sources to attribute see above)","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Salento","place":"Salento, Quindío","at":[4.6373,-75.5